*  Rem was
*    CREATE.ACCOUNT acc.name pathname {NO.QUERY}
*  Now 
*    CREATE.ACCOUNT USER <user acct name>  {ADMINISTRATOR} {NO.QUERY}  - account created in  /home/sd/user_accounts/<user acct name>  owner:group set to <username>:"sdu_"+<username>
*                                                 <username> must be found in sdusers group!
*
*    ADMINISTRATOR (14 Aug 26, Windows port) makes the account an SD
*    administrator by putting it in Windows Administrators - which since
*    PROJECT_STATUS.md 5.6.1 is the whole of what being an SD administrator
*    means.  Omit it and the account is a standard local user, which is the
*    default and the common case.  It cannot be abbreviated; see more.args.
*
*    PROGRAMMER (17 Aug 26, Windows port) gives the account the FULL VOC -
*    compiler, cataloguer, editors and the shell verbs.  Without it, and
*    without ADMINISTRATOR, the account is a STANDARD one and gets NEWVOC less
*    the verbs named in NEWVOC's TIER.OMIT.STANDARD record: it can run an
*    application but not build one.  ADMINISTRATOR implies PROGRAMMER.
*    PROJECT_STATUS.md section 8.
*
*    THE THREE TIERS AND WHERE EACH VOC COMES FROM (17 Aug 26, Windows port):
*      STANDARD       NEWVOC less TIER.OMIT.STANDARD
*      PROGRAMMER     NEWVOC entire
*      ADMINISTRATOR  NEWVOC entire, plus the records named in
*                     TIER.ADD.ADMINISTRATOR, read from VOC_TEMPLATE
*    Owner's ruling, 17 Aug 2026: "administrators get the whole voc".  The nine
*    administration verbs live in VOC_TEMPLATE alone, so before this an SD
*    administrator had to LOGTO SDSYS to reach any of them.
*
*    THE TIER IS WRITTEN TO ACCOUNTS FIELD 5 (ACC$TIER) and LOGIN reads it back.
*    Without that record the reduction lasted only until the release stamp moved:
*    LOGIN's update.voc re-copies the whole of NEWVOC, and it is reached from an
*    ordinary login by a prompt anybody can answer Y to.
*
*    NONE OF THE THREE IS A WALL.  An administrator can copy any verb into any
*    account's VOC afterwards (owner, 17 Aug 2026), so the reduced VOC is the
*    posture an account starts in, not a boundary anything enforces.  The
*    boundary that does exist is the operating system's, and section 8 records
*    that OS.EXECUTE ... CAPTURING is ungated regardless of any of this.
*    CREATE.ACCOUNT GROUP <grp acct name>  {NO.QUERY}  - account created in  /home/sd/group_accounts/<grp acct name> owner:group set to sdsys:group_name
*                                                        Note - users will need to be added to group with MODIFY.ACCOUNT ADD group_name username
*    CREATE.ACCOUNT OTHER acc.name pathname {NO.QUERY} - account created in pathname, maintained for backwards compatiblilty. This will require manual editing
*                                                        of the accounts record to specify linux group the account belongs to.
